  3. Performance

  expenseList.map() in ExpenseList.tsx renders the mobile card list AND the desktop table — both always rendered, hidden via CSS     
  (block sm:hidden / hidden sm:block). On a page with 100 expenses, you're rendering every expense twice. Use a proper useMediaQuery 
  hook and render only one list:

  const isMobile = useMediaQuery('(max-width: 640px)');
  return isMobile ? <MobileExpenseList ... /> : <DesktopExpenseTable ... />;

  today computed on module load (PersonalExpenseDashboard.tsx:43)

  const today = new Date().toISOString().split('T')[0]; // module-level constant

  This is computed once when the module is first imported. If the app stays open past midnight, today is stale. Move it into the     
  component body or use a useMemo with a date-change watcher.

  AddExpense.tsx — URL.createObjectURL leaks

  URL.createObjectURL(file) on line 243 creates an object URL that's never revoked. On every receipt file change the old URL leaks.  
  Add a cleanup effect:

  useEffect(() => {
    return () => {
      if (form.receiptPreview.startsWith('blob:')) {
        URL.revokeObjectURL(form.receiptPreview);
      }
    };
  }, [form.receiptPreview]);

  validateForm duplicates isValid logic (AddExpense.tsx:182-199, 218-224)

  There are two separate validity computations: validateForm() and the isValid boolean derived inline. They can get out of sync      
  (e.g., validateForm checks hasReceipt && !receipt but isValid doesn't). One source of truth:

  const formErrors = useMemo(() => validateForm(form), [form]);
  const isValid = Object.keys(formErrors).length === 0;

  ---
  4. Responsiveness & Layout

  ExpenseList.tsx:84 — w-[25%] on the AddExpense wrapper

  <div className='flex-1 w-[25%]'>
    <AddExpense ... />
  </div>

  AddExpense is a fixed-position modal (fixed inset-0). Putting it inside a w-[25%] div is meaningless — fixed elements are taken out
   of flow. Remove the wrapper entirely.

  OtpVerificationPage.tsx:147 — broken clamp

  sx={{ fontSize: 'clamp(1rem, 5vw, 0.75rem)' }}

  The min value (1rem) is larger than the max value (0.75rem). clamp(min, preferred, max) requires min ≤ max. This always resolves to
   1rem on most displays. It should be clamp(0.75rem, 2vw, 1rem).

  Dashboard layout — PersonalExpenseDashboard wraps cards in max-w-5xl but the expense table section has max-w-6xl. This creates a   
  slight width inconsistency. Pick one max-width for the whole page container and apply it at the page level.

  BottomNav overlaps content — The bottom nav is h-16 fixed at the bottom, but no bottom padding is applied to the page content. On  
  mobile, the last visible row of the expense table will be hidden behind the nav bar.

  ---
  5. UI/UX Evaluation

  The search bar does nothing. (ExpenseList.tsx:93-101)

  There's a search input with a placeholder "Search Expense" and a label for accessibility, but no onChange, no filtering logic, no  
  state connected to it. It's completely non-functional UI. Either implement it or remove it — showing users a search box that does  
  nothing destroys trust.

  OTP expired → submit button repurposed as "request new OTP" (OtpVerificationPage.tsx:100-105)

  When isTimerExpired, clicking "Submit" calls requestOtp() instead of submitting. The button still says "Submit". This is
  disorienting. The UI should show the expired state clearly and have a dedicated "Resend OTP" button rather than hijacking the      
  submit action.

  Modal feedback is orange regardless of error type (Modal.tsx:7)

  bg-[#F2994A] (orange) is used for all notifications — errors, success ("OTP sent to your email"), and auth failures. Orange reads  
  as a warning. Use green for success, red for errors.

  <Link href="/register"> instead of <Link to="/register"> (LoginPage.tsx:180)

  MUI's Link with href does a full page reload. In a SPA this breaks state and is slower. Use React Router's Link component or pass  
  component={RouterLink} to MUI Link. Same issue in RegisterUserPage.tsx:234.

  No loading state on OTP resend (OtpVerificationPage.tsx:68-98)

  The requestOtp function fires an axios request with no loading indicator. The user can click "Here" multiple times and spam the    
  endpoint. Add a loading state and disable the link during the request.

  Delete expense has no confirmation (ExpenseList.tsx:167)

  onClick={() => void deleteExpenseMutation(expense.expenseId ?? '')}

  A single click permanently deletes an expense with no confirmation dialog. This is a destructive action that users will
  accidentally trigger. Add a confirmation step.

  ---
  6. Typography

  Three font families in play with no clear hierarchy:
  - IBM Plex Sans — hardcoded in Otp.tsx:188 (styled component, not from Tailwind config)
  - Inter — defined in tailwind.config.js
  - Poppins — defined in tailwind.config.js, used with font-poppins class in ExpenseList.tsx:102
  - MUI components use its own default Roboto

  You have four fonts loading. None of this is coordinated. The Tailwind config defines the fonts but they're not enforced as a base 
  style in index.css. MUI uses Roboto unless configured to use Inter. Pick one font family, set it globally via both the Tailwind    
  fontFamily.sans override and MUI's createTheme({ typography: { fontFamily: '...' } }).

  clamp font sizing is inconsistently applied — some MUI Typography components use clamp, others use fixed variant sizes. This makes 
  text scaling unpredictable across viewports.

  Dashboard body text is consistently text-sm / text-xs — the information density is high, but there's no clear typographic scale.   
  Card titles, amounts, labels, and descriptions all sit within a 11px–24px range with no systematic hierarchy defined in config.    

