  7. Color System

  Two completely separate color systems:

  The auth pages use MUI's default theme (blues, grays, white background). The dashboard uses a dark custom palette (#121215,        
  #17171c, #1f1f24, #2a2a30, teal #009689). These are never connected.

  All dark theme colors are hardcoded magic strings:
  #121215  #17171c  #1f1f24  #2a2a30  #3d3d45  #005a52

  These appear scattered across multiple files. If you ever want to adjust the base dark color, you'd need to grep-replace across the
   codebase. Move these to tailwind.config.js:

  theme: {
    extend: {
      colors: {
        surface: {
          base: '#121215',
          card: '#17171c',
          hover: '#1f1f24',
          elevated: '#2a2a30',
        },
        brand: {
          DEFAULT: '#009689',
          dark: '#005a52',
        },
      },
    },
  },

  WCAG contrast failures:
  - text-zinc-500 on bg-[#17171c] — #71717a on #17171c gives approximately 4.5:1. Passes AA for normal text, fails for small text.   
  - text-zinc-600 (#52525b) on #17171c — approximately 3.2:1. Fails AA entirely. This is used for expense.description
  (ExpenseList.tsx:149) — secondary information that's actually unreadable.
  - The orange modal bg-[#F2994A] with text-white — orange/white combinations are notoriously low contrast. At this saturation it's  
  approximately 2.8:1. Fails AA.

  The teal brand color is inconsistent: #009689 (Tailwind class bg-[#009689]) and Tailwind's teal-600 (#0d9488) are both used and are
   visually different. The category selection active state uses teal-600/teal-400 from Tailwind while the Add button uses #009689.   
  Pick one.

