  8. Spacing & Visual Consistency

  ExpenseList.tsx table vs mobile card layout have different padding standards:
  - Table cells: px-6 py-4 / px-6 py-3
  - Mobile cards: px-4 py-3

  Neither is wrong, but the inconsistency between layouts for the same data means the product feels like two different apps on mobile
   vs desktop.

  AddExpense.tsx has a gap-4 grid that switches to gap-2 inside the category grid — fine, but the category buttons use px-2 py-2     
  while the notes textarea and other inputs use px-3 py-2. The inconsistency is subtle but visible when looking at alignment.        

  DashBoardCards.tsx uses p-3 sm:p-5 while the rest of the dashboard uses a fixed 4px-based scale. The p-3 (12px) → p-5 (20px) jump  
  is non-standard. Consider p-4 sm:p-6.

